Spec: Authenticated FRP service composition

Purpose:
  Route actual backend requests through device/application authority without a legacy admission bypass.

Owns:
  ./linkgate.go
  ./linkgate_test.go

References:
  /control-plane/authority/transport_gate.sdd

Must:
  Enter secure mode only during service construction, disable alternate listeners/plugins/public proxies and require the real Agent TLS scope before FRP decoding.
  Preserve authenticated scope through multiplexing and message wrappers, match login user/client namespace, and bind work/visitor RunIDs to actual peers.
  Permit simultaneous private runtimes within the same authenticated namespace using a canonical lowercase `128`-bit instance suffix on client ID; the suffix grants no cross-application or cross-role authority.
  Register only stcp/xtcp publications with approved service metadata and deterministic names, close failed registrations, and close live relay sockets on authorization cancellation.
  Bound asynchronous hole-punch work in separate visitor and response lanes, and check actual visitor/client/report identity for every live session.
  Preserve existing unauthenticated legacy behavior only when the new secure composition is not selected.
  Bound transaction/session identifiers and numeric IP/port candidate arrays before analysis; malformed candidates cannot enter the hole-punch analyzer.
  Keep standard TLS handshakes off the accept loop with at most thirty-two accepted handshake workers; a silent unauthenticated peer cannot block the next valid device.
